{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לעפרן", :translit "l'efron", :gloss "to Ephron"} {:he "עין רע", :translit "ayin ra", :gloss "evil eye"} {:he "עפרן", :translit "efron", :gloss "Ephron"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "עפרן", :b "ת'"}], :frame {:text "Ephron's name is written defective (לעפרן without the vav) in Genesis 23:16. The defective spelling reduces his numeric total so that עפרן equals exactly 400, the number of shekels Abraham paid for the Cave of Machpelah (Genesis 23:15–16). The phrase עין רע characterizes Ephron's greed: he initially offered the field for free but then demanded the full inflated price (Genesis 23:11–15).", :sources ["Genesis 23:15" "Genesis 23:16" "Genesis 23:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "עפרן", :a-value 400, :b "ת'", :b-value 400, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:26.585010422Z", :model "glm-5.2"}